From dcc23b697e8e63e318cf3d746e4348faa28b5d1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:31:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] power: supply: apple: keep J71t charging steady across
 USB link PM

Keep the owner budget through suspend and a five-second reset grace
instead of revoking it with the instantaneous gadget budget. Tristar
reports the enumerated 500 mA source while suspended, including when the
gadget zeros current_ma. Preserve the analog detector's connected/host-
grant guard.

Apply battery then input limits directly, without an input-suspend
ritual. Ramp 500/1000/2100/2400 mA at most once per second and retry
elevation after 30 seconds following a step-down. Arm the validated
owner limit at probe. Only explicit zero or confirmed VBUS loss revokes
that authorization.

Treat gauge presence/cache and transport errors as transient, preserving
an active budget for at most 60 seconds without valid safety samples. A
valid pack voltage proves presence when bq27xxx PRESENT is zero. Use a
45 C trip and 42 C clear with a 500 mA thermal floor.
Timeout/termination also step down. Only register-ownership mismatches
latch, with a guarded 60-second retry.

Validated with actual-function ASan/UBSan timing and fault injection
tests, USB resume/ECM regressions, gadget budget assertions, and Tristar
mux faults. No device access or syscfg/NVRAM writes.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
